record.statement:
Classify real linear combinations of products of minors that are
	nonnegative for all $TN$ matrices. More concretely, given a
	polynomial $p( \{ x_{I \times J} \ | \ I,J \subset [n], |I| = |J| \}
	)$, when can one certify, via some constructive algorithmic process, that evaluating $p$ at $x_{I \times J} =
	\det A_{I \times J}$ yields a non-negative output for all $TN$
	matrices $A$.
